total war warhammer 3 might have the  best battles we've seen so far  in this long beloved franchise alongside  the new factions unit story and  everything else that comes with new  entries to the series there are also  massive new narrative style survival  battles which is what i got hands on  with recently these survival battles  exist  as big narrative landmarks through the  campaigns of total war warhammer 3.  so whether you're playing as kislev cafe  or one of the forces of chaos  you'll be taken to these cursed fields  as part of the main questline they're  designed to feel like big  important and memorable battles and from  what i've played  they seem to be really nailing it  warriors of kislev  we have travelled far and  but at last we have arrived in corn's  bloody realm  before us stands the bra citadel  where the blood god's gatekeeper stands  guard  we must call out the fiend and slay him  they died  the idea behind them is that your  faction is invading the realms of the  chaos gods  and in the gameplay you can see right  now i'm playing as kislev under the  command of the tsarina catarin  against the hordes of corn the god of  blood and skulls  which will go some way to explaining the  decor choices in this crimson neck of  the woods  while we are yet to see them there will  be other survival battles that take  place in the other three realms as well  so expect to see gross pus and boils for  nurgle tentacles and  excess for slaanesh and physics i don't  know  clocks anyway these long wars of  attrition start with you bringing in a  force into the realm of chaos  and advancing as you take strategic  objectives one at a time  until finally a greater demon approaches  for the final showdown  cons gatekeeper shows himself at last  warriors of kislev prepare for the fight  of your lives  now once you take one of these  objectives the battle switches from you  assaulting points  to putting up a desperate defense to  assist you in holding on to your new  fielded prize  with each point taken you as the player  are able to summon more units  build strong defenses heal and resupply  or buff your existing forces  all paid for with a currency called  supply which is earned by taking victory  points and defeating demons and  nerdwells this is where i feel the  battles  really shine through and present  themselves as a fresh new way to wage  war within the total war franchise  because you don't have enough supply to  do everything you want you really have  to stay on your feet with the strategies  you employ  when it comes to defending your strong  point or lean into the play style you  feel most comfortable with  all of this in order to give yourself  every advantage possible  as you face off some truly overwhelming  odds  some of the building options available  to your defensive force include among  others  a selection of towers flinging arrows or  bolts of magic  stall walls to cut off approaches firing  platforms to allow your range units to  fire down death  traps to slow and wound the enemy and  idols that buff allied forces that stay  within their field  this is a great new option if you're  someone like me who leans into a  defensive play style  making the most of choke points  strengthening your position favoring  units with high defense  and using your cossa or strategy gun and  axe units to take down enemies on their  approach  with your walls and towers you can  create your very own bottlenecks and  force the enemy to fight where you want  them now they can take down these  defenses but if they bunch up and start  hacking away at your walls  well thankfully your general and ice  mage have some pretty  devastating area of effect spells to  have those berserkers shattering  alternatively you can spend your  resources on kitting out your units with  higher tier weapons and armor  to make your smaller fighting force  really pack a punch  this sort of tower defense gameplay adds  a new wrinkle to battles  and being able to use the terrain to  your advantage and turn enemy points  into fortifications of your own really  is important when it comes to balancing  the attack and defense dynamic of the  survival battles  but it is also important to bear the  fight ahead in mind  when you sell fortifications you get a  few resources back and allow you to  shift focus to the skirmishes ahead of  you  these battles are taking place behind  enemy lines and  in unfamiliar territory that means you  can expect to have demons  constantly spawning behind you and  taking the fight to your flanks  usually this will result in you having  to split your force and fight on  multiple fronts  testing the micromanaging abilities of  any commander because as this fight  progresses  and you get access to bigger and better  units like the elemental bear and grom  cannons so too will the demons of corn  try their best to throw  their considerable weight around meaning  that by the end of these battles you're  likely beset on all fronts  scrambling together what little  resources you have to heal repair and  reinforce exhausted forces  all while greater demons skull crushers  and angry lads with names like skarg  fleshmaul try to turn your femurs into  toothpicks  this crescendo of battle you work  towards really feels like a worthwhile  payoff  to the drawn out invasions that will  mostly last players at least  40 minutes  he is  dash  total war has always created some really  exciting climactic experiences to their  quest battles  but the ebb and flow of these survival  battles alongside the wealth of  customizable options  really works in creating something new  for the series  the new battle setting of the brass  citadel as well as some of the awesome  new units of kislev and corn were really  exciting to get my hands on  and honestly as a huge total war and  warhammer fan i can't wait to play more  of this final installment of the series  but personally it was the survival  battles themselves that really stood out  to me  whether you're fighting through them  solo in your campaign or bringing in  your friends as allies and playing them  co-op online  i hope other total war fans out there  are as excited for the survival battles  as i am if you enjoyed this video be  sure to like it tell me your thoughts of  these battles in the comments section  down below i'll be in the comments  section as soon as this video goes live  to answer as many questions as i can  and for more of your virtual warhammer  fix be sure to subscribe  to gamespot my brave kiss levites  we stand triumphant but corn is not the  only dark god with a realm in this  accursed place  the battle is won but the war goes on  come we must continue our search  for what is lost  you
 

